      "text": "<@307290318590705667> so the refineries aren't broken, here's the math for Bion. aluminium refinery = 64 base x 1.45 productivity x 1.104 specialisation x 0.39 workforce efficiency = 40.2. the 0.39 is the nation-wide one: your buildings need about 824M workers (steel mills 378M, geothermal 193M, farms 150M, component factories 100M) and you only have 323M jobs filled, so everything you make runs at 39% even buildings that employ no workers. vertical integration is 0 because it only counts bauxite mines in the same province as the refineries, mines in other provinces don't count. more working pop/education or fewer worker-heavy buildings brings it up"
